UNIVERSAL GRADER (odd-girth / cyclicity) on TOURNAMENTS -- transitive=inf=orderable, intransitive=3:
  n=4: 4 iso classes; (#3-cycles, odd-girth) = [(0, 'inf'), (1, 3), (1, 3), (2, 3)]
  n=5: 12 iso classes; (#3-cycles, odd-girth) = [(0, 'inf'), (1, 3), (1, 3), (1, 3), (2, 3), (2, 3), (3, 3), (3, 3), (4, 3), (4, 3), (4, 3), (5, 3)]
  => n=4 (the Klein four): the TRANSITIVE class has odd-girth inf (orderable=the cusp); the others
     have odd-girth 3 (Condorcet). The SAME grader (odd-girth) that gives the apex doublet girth 7
     and difference-sets girth 3 grades tournaments by orderability -- one invariant, all objects.
